{"change_summary":"Added a `legacy_pre_stage_state_json` helper in `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` so schema v2/v3 migration tests build real pre-stage animal payloads and strip schema-6-only fields before migration. I also aligned the save-load reserve assertions with the current stage-cohort model by checking `AnimalState::total_reserve_g()` and the `animal.total_reserve_g` invariant. The weekly trim/export regression already used `animal.adult.count` and `animal.juvenile.count`, so it required validation rather than another code change.","outstanding_risks":["I did not rerun the full `tank_core` test suite; validation covered `save_load` and the targeted 500-hour trim/export regression."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the trim/export regression and confirmed it already uses the stage-cohort animal API in the current branch.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Added a reusable legacy pre-stage save fixture helper and rewired the schema v2/v3 migration tests to use flat-animal payloads without schema-6-only fields.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated save-load reserve expectations to use `AnimalState::total_reserve_g()` and the current `animal.total_reserve_g` invariant name.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran the save-load regression suite and the targeted 500-hour trim-and-remove regression.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load` passed (21 tests).","`cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load legacy_schema_v4_saves_migrate_trim_plants_to_trim_and_remove -- --exact` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking test_weekly_trim_and_remove_exports_nutrients_over_500_hours -- --exact` passed."]}